sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) chemotactic stripe splitting & stripe-spot selection — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py` (91.4/100, up from 54.4/100 in Pass 1; +37.0 overall). The remediated script integrates the nonlinear 1D and 2D Keller-Segel-Painter chemotactic-reaction-diffusion PDE system dn/dt = D_n Lap(n) - div(n chi(c) grad(c)) + r n (1 - n/n_0), dc/dt = D_c Lap(c) + alpha n / (1 + beta n) - gamma c at equal diffusivity D_n = D_c = 1.0, verifying the analytical chemotactic threshold chi_c = 4.5 (chi_eff_c = 9.0) and critical wavelength lambda_c = pi * sqrt(2) = 4.4429 with 0.000% simulated wavelength error across the 5-regime domain-growth cascade (N = 1, 2, 4, 8 stripes for s = 1, 2, 4, 8 and N = 0 for subcritical control chi = 3.0 < chi_c, RMSE = 0.0000), continuous growing-domain stripe splitting (1 -> 2 -> 4 stripes), 2D cubic labyrinthine stripe vs quadratic spot selection, and automated CV segmentation of the CC BY-SA 4.0 Myxococcus xanthus specimen (`chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg`, 4 fruiting bodies, rippling stripe wavelength 74.10 um = 18.52 px, CV = 0.3459), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_005_chemotactic_stripe_splitting.lean`. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 91.0, reproducibility 91.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/chemotactic_stripe_splitting_comparison.png: rendered output of 1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 900896 B, 2310×1372 px, artifact_sha256 c37361ad1d68ce676ba2e1cd9c205a97927c6ad87e8d8ed4de517b9bcb4418a7 (sha256 c37361ad1d68ce676ba2e1cd9c205a97927c6ad87e8d8ed4de517b9bcb4418a7), spec_fingerprint 91fb31037b136e4adc1e8bdd7b6c8097f7eaab327a03b1266cf7114f22d5f57f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 91fb31037b136e4adc1e8bdd7b6c8097f7eaab327a03b1266cf7114f22d5f57f; artifact_sha256: c37361ad1d68ce676ba2e1cd9c205a97927c6ad87e8d8ed4de517b9bcb4418a7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/chemotactic_stripe_splitting/chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg=7b1780ffcb70f313..., datasets/chemotactic_stripe_splitting/chemotactic_stripe_splitting_reference.json=2c37ed1ab3d26a08..., datasets/chemotactic_stripe_splitting/scout_manifest.json=4b4e20a991f65c81...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) PNAS 96(10):5549-5554 Keller-Segel chemotactic-reaction-diffusion equations, equal-diffusivity instability threshold chi > chi_c at D_n = D_c, domain-growth stripe-splitting cascade, and 2D stripe vs spot selection | Keller & Segel (1970) J. Theor. Biol. 26:399-415 chemotactic flux cross-diffusion -div(n chi(c) grad(c)); reconstructed_in_script: 1D and 2D IMEX pseudospectral Keller-Segel-Painter PDE solvers across stationary domain scales s in {1, 2, 4, 8}, subcritical chemotaxis control chi = 3.0 < chi_c = 4.5, exponentially growing domain kymograph (1 -> 2 -> 4 stripes), and 2D cubic labyrinthine stripes vs quadratic spot droplets | Computer-vision segmentation of Myxococcus xanthus specimen (`chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0) extracting 4 fruiting-body spot aggregates and 362 chemotactic rippling stripe spacings (74.10 um mean wavelength calibrated via 500 um = 125 px scale bar); transfer_boundary: 1D growing domain and 2D planar chemotactic PDE mapped to Myxococcus xanthus rippling stripe ridges and fruiting-body spot aggregates; does_not_claim: Individual-cell C-signal contact-reversal mechanics or 3D viscoelastic fruiting-body stalk elevation." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple cell density n(x,t) to an explicit extracellular slime-trail orientation tensor for Myxococcus xanthus social gliding motility.",
            "remediation needed: Extend the 2D chemotactic PDE to a growing curved surface to model vertebrate skin and fish pigment stripe bifurcations alongside bacterial rippling." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.913"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

